--- body ---
## Context

On the 2026-11-09 RDJHSS data-paper release (CNRS session), the agent
reached the HAL step of REALF How-to 44 and could not load
`update-publist`: `disable-model-invocation: true` refused the Skill call
and told the agent to ask the author to type `/update-publist`. The author
typed it; the same agent then ran the same procedure. The flag bought a
round trip, not a protection: the protection lives inside the skill, whose
own gates stop before `make sync` and before every SWORD call until the
author confirms the displayed payload.

Author instruction in that session: "Fix the harness, allow agent", then
"Your channel to harness fixing is a ticket" — the direct PR (#2317) was
withdrawn and this ticket replaces it. Related: 1483 (`/fly` lifecycle
skill), which will delegate the page and HAL steps to this skill and needs
it loadable.

## Proposed change

- `skills/update-publist/SKILL.md`: `disable-model-invocation: false`.
  Keep `user-invocable: true` and every confirmation gate in the body.
- `skills/submission-event/SKILL.md` (or `fly` after 1483): drop the
  "explicit-only" wording and the instruction to ask the author to invoke
  it; say instead to load it and follow its gates.
- Alternative considered and set aside: an allow-list hook on `make sync`
  and the SWORD URLs, heavier than gates the skill already enforces.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] An agent can load `update-publist` through the Skill tool
- [ ] The skill still asks for explicit confirmation before `make sync` and before each non-dry-run SWORD call (text unchanged there)
- [ ] `submission-event`/`fly` no longer tells the agent to hand the invocation back to the author
- [ ] `tests/test_skill_frontmatter.py`, `test_skill_descriptions.py`, `test_gen_skills_catalog.py` pass

## Imagine + Plan (raid a8b3e4, 2026-11-09)

Premise: PR #2325 replaced `submission-event` with `paper` (the planned `fly`
became `paper`, ticket 1483). Criteria 1, 2, 4 hold on the tree
(`skills/update-publist/SKILL.md` still `disable-model-invocation: true`).
Criterion 3 now reads on `skills/paper/SKILL.md` § Written once: it already
says "load it and follow its gates" but keeps the fallback "if the runtime
refuses the load, ask the author to type it", which is the hand-back to drop.
Not voided; mapped, wording of the criterion left as filed.

Actions: flip the flag; replace paper's fallback clause; leave every
confirmation gate paragraph byte-identical; run the three named tests (no
description change, so no catalog regeneration). The log note on HAL PUT
(`Content-Disposition` filename must be the XML name for a zip PUT) gets one
note in § 2c outside the gate paragraphs; the POST example is left as is
(evidence covers PUT only).

Blind spot: a loadable skill can be loaded in a subagent, whose "user" is
its parent agent; the gate text says "user". No hook guards `make sync` or
SWORD. Criterion 2 forbids touching the gate text, so paper's replacement
sentence says to load update-publist in the session that talks with the
author, never in a delegated worker.
